{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-christoffel-symbols-second-kind","title":"def:pet-ch2-christoffel-symbols-second-kind","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":655,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#def:pet-ch2-christoffel-symbols-second-kind","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-metric-coordinate-formulas]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"def:pet-ch2-christoffel-symbols-second-kind","line":1320,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Christoffel symbols of the second kind]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch2-christoffel-symbols-second-kind}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0084}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor, def:pet-ch2-metric-coordinate-formulas}\n\n  In local coordinates, expand\n  $\\nabla_YX=Y^i\\big(\\partial_i(X^j)\\big)\\partial_j+Y^iX^j\\Gamma^k_{ij}\\partial_k$, where\n  $\\Gamma^k_{ij}$, the \\emph{Christoffel symbols of the second kind}, are\n  defined by $\\nabla_{\\partial_i}\\partial_j=\\Gamma^k_{ij}\\partial_k$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Christoffel symbols of the second kind] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d6368726973746f6666656c2d73796d626f6c732d7365636f6e642d6b696e64\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0084</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor\">↗ def:pet-ch2-co